## 3. RENDERING OPTIMIZATION PLAN

### 3.1 The 1-Second Timer Re-Render Storm

```
CURRENT FLOW (every second when clocked in):
  setInterval (1000ms)
    → setElapsedTimer(new string)
    → DashboardLayout re-renders (573 lines)
    → Sidebar re-renders (14 nav items)
    → TopBar re-renders
    → Clock widget re-renders
    → {children} (Outlet) re-renders
    → Current page component re-renders
    → All child components of current page re-render

RESULT: 60 full-tree re-renders per minute for every user who is clocked in.

FIX STRATEGY:
  1. Extract timer into isolated <ClockTimer> component
  2. Use React.memo on Sidebar, TopBar, and Outlet wrapper
  3. Timer state stays local to <ClockTimer> — parent never re-renders
  4. Timer uses requestAnimationFrame instead of setInterval for better perf
  
ESTIMATED IMPACT: 99% reduction in unnecessary re-renders
```

