## 4. STATE MANAGEMENT STRATEGY

### 4.1 Current State Architecture

```
CURRENT:
  Module-level globals: globalProfile, globalClockedIn, globalLogId, globalBadges
  Component-level useState: 10-15 state variables per page component
  No shared state management library
  No query caching
  Every page fetches its own profile from supabase.auth.getUser() + profiles.select
  
PROBLEMS:
  ✗ Profile fetched 3-5 times per navigation (DashboardLayout + page + sub-components)
  ✗ Global mutables are not reactive — updates don't trigger re-renders in other components
  ✗ No cache invalidation — stale data served until full page refresh
  ✗ No optimistic updates — every action waits for DB round-trip
  ✗ Role stored in 3 places: user_metadata, profiles table, and component prop
```

### 4.2 Recommended Architecture: TanStack Query + Zustand

```
LAYER 1: TanStack Query (Server State — DB data)
  Purpose: Fetch, cache, and synchronize all Supabase data
  Benefits:
    - Automatic caching with configurable staleTime
    - Background refetching
    - Deduplication (same query from 3 components = 1 API call)
    - Optimistic updates for mutations
    - Pagination/infinite scroll built-in
    
  Example:
    const { data: profile } = useQuery({
      queryKey: ['profile', userId],
      queryFn: () => supabase.from('profiles').select('*').eq('id', userId).single(),
      staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes
    });

LAYER 2: Zustand (Client State — UI state)
  Purpose: Clock state, sidebar toggle, active modals, UI preferences
  Benefits:
    - Replaces global mutable variables with reactive store
    - No provider nesting (unlike React Context)
    - Selective subscription (component subscribes to specific slice)
    - DevTools support
    
  Store design:
    useAppStore: { clockedIn, logId, clockInTime, workLocation }
    useUIStore: { sidebarOpen, activeModal, theme }
    useAuthStore: { profile, role, isAuthenticated }

WHY NOT:
  ✗ Redux: Overkill boilerplate for this scale; TanStack Query handles server state
  ✗ React Context: Causes full sub-tree re-render on any value change
  ✗ Zustand alone: Not designed for async server state (no caching, refetching)
  ✗ MobX: Learning curve + complex observables
```

### 4.3 Migration Path

```
Phase A: Install TanStack Query + Zustand
Phase B: Create useAuthStore (replace globalProfile, globalClockedIn, etc.)
Phase C: Create query hooks (useProfile, useLeaves, useApplications, etc.)
Phase D: Migrate pages one-by-one from useState+useEffect to useQuery
Phase E: Remove all raw supabase.from().select() calls from components
```

