## 10. CACHING ARCHITECTURE

### 10.1 Multi-Layer Caching Strategy

```
LAYER 1: TanStack Query (Client-Side)
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Cache Key          │ staleTime    │ gcTime       │
  ├────────────────────┼──────────────┼──────────────┤
  │ ['profile', id]    │ 5 min        │ 30 min       │
  │ ['dashboard']      │ 30 sec       │ 5 min        │
  │ ['applications', page] │ 1 min    │ 10 min       │
  │ ['badges']         │ 10 sec       │ 1 min        │
  │ ['org_metrics']    │ 5 min        │ 30 min       │
  │ ['payroll', month] │ 10 min       │ 1 hour       │
  │ ['notifications']  │ 15 sec       │ 5 min        │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  
  Invalidation triggers:
    Realtime event on table X → invalidate queries keyed to X

LAYER 2: Database Views (Server-Side)
  Regular views: Computed on read (always fresh)
  Materialized views: Pre-computed, refreshed on schedule
    mv_department_headcount: REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY every 15 min
    mv_monthly_attrition: REFRESH daily at 00:00 UTC

LAYER 3: Edge Function Response Cache (Vercel)
  AI proxy responses: Cache-Control: max-age=300 (5 min for same input)
  Assessment grading: No cache (unique per submission)
